# build output
inky-oled/build/
*.idsig

# The built dashboard APK. Deliberately NOT tracked: build.ps1 bakes assets/config.js
# straight into it, so a locally built APK contains the owner's real coordinates. A zipped
# APK is a binary, and the pre-commit secret scanner only reads text — it cannot see inside
# one. Build it with inky-oled/build.ps1 instead of committing it.
inky-oled/inkyoled.apk

# assets/config.js stays TRACKED (it is the placeholder template everyone starts from) but
# local edits to it are held back with:
#     git update-index --skip-worktree inky-oled/assets/config.js
# so a real location never lands in a commit. If you ever need to change the committed
# template, --no-skip-worktree, edit, verify the diff contains no real coordinates, commit,
# then re-apply --skip-worktree.

# signing key — never commit
*.keystore
debug.keystore

# AOSP sources pulled for research (Apache-2.0, Google copyright).
# Not vendored here — research/README.md has the exact URLs to re-fetch them.
research/DisplayDeviceConfig.java
research/HdrBrightnessData.java
research/display-device-config.xsd

# Working log — kept local. Contains device serials, account emails and LAN IPs.
# The README carries the condensed, publishable version of the findings.
PROGRESS.md
*-progress.md

# reports generated on-device (contain serials / identifiers)
*-report.txt
speaker-report.txt
battery-report.txt
patches/D-kiosk-settings/backup.json

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
